[32m+[m[32m# Contributing[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFocalDesk is currently a solo-developed alpha project. Contributions, bug[m
[32m+[m[32mreports, and design feedback may be welcome, but there is no formal maintainer[m
[32m+[m[32mteam, release process, or guaranteed review timeline yet.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Project Status[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFocalDesk is experimental compositor and desktop environment software. Expect[m
[32m+[m[32mbreaking changes, incomplete features, and architectural churn.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBefore contributing, read the [README](README.md) for the current project shape[m
[32m+[m[32mand build instructions.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Issues[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUse issues for:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Reproducible bugs.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Build or setup failures.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Clear feature requests.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Design questions that need a durable record.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen reporting a bug, include:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- What you expected to happen.[m
[32m+[m[32m- What actually happened.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Steps to reproduce the problem.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Your Linux distribution, desktop/session context, GPU driver, and relevant[m
[32m+[m[32m  Wayland environment details when applicable.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Logs or terminal output when useful.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDo not include security-sensitive details in public issues. See[m
[32m+[m[32m[SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) for vulnerability reporting guidance.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Pull Requests[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBecause the project is early and currently maintained by one person, small,[m
[32m+[m[32mfocused pull requests are much easier to review than broad rewrites.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGood pull requests usually:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Solve one problem at a time.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Match the existing Rust style and project structure.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Include tests when the change touches behavior that can be tested.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Avoid unrelated formatting, refactors, or dependency changes.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Explain the user-visible impact or architectural reason for the change.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mLarge architectural changes should start as an issue or discussion before code is[m
[32m+[m[32mwritten.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Development Checks[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBefore opening a pull request, run the relevant checks when possible:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```sh[m
[32m+[m[32mcargo fmt --all -- --check[m
[32m+[m[32mcargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings[m
[32m+[m[32mcargo test --workspace[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf a check cannot be run locally, mention that in the pull request.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Coding Guidelines[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Prefer simple, explicit Rust over premature abstraction.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Keep compositor, IPC, permissions, and portal-related changes especially[m
[32m+[m[32m  conservative.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Follow the existing crate boundaries unless there is a clear reason to change[m
[32m+[m[32m  them.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Treat input handling, process launching, file access, IPC, and automation as[m
[32m+[m[32m  security-sensitive areas.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Keep user-facing behavior predictable and recoverable, especially for alpha[m
[32m+[m[32m  features.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Maintainer Notes[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAt this stage, the project direction may change quickly. A contribution being[m
[32m+[m[32mtechnically sound does not guarantee it fits the current roadmap.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mReview and merge decisions are ultimately made by the project owner.[m
