[32m+[m[32m# FocalDesk[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFocalDesk is an alpha desktop environment project built around a custom Wayland compositor and a cohesive system experience layer.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe long-term direction is a fast, keyboard-friendly, retro-futuristic desktop with structured workspaces, clear system feedback, and permissioned automation. See [docs/vision.md](docs/vision.md) for the broader project direction.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Status[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFocalDesk is alpha software.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIt is stable enough for daily use by the project owner, but it is still early in[m
[32m+[m[32mdevelopment. Expect incomplete features, breaking changes, rough edges, and[m
[32m+[m[32moccasional compositor-level bugs. If you try it as a daily driver, be prepared[m
[32m+[m[32mto debug Linux desktop, Wayland, graphics, and input issues.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Repository Layout[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `apps/focaldesk-desktop`: compositor executable[m
[32m+[m[32m- `apps/focaldesk-cli`: command-line interface[m
[32m+[m[32m- `apps/focaldesk-files`: file app prototype[m
[32m+[m[32m- `apps/focaldesk-settings`: settings app prototype[m
[32m+[m[32m- `apps/focaldesk-portal`: portal-related app code[m
[32m+[m[32m- `services/focaldesk-server`: background server and IPC daemon[m
[32m+[m[32m- `crates/`: shared FocalDesk libraries[m
[32m+[m[32m- `assets/`: bundled visual assets[m
[32m+[m[32m- `docs/`: design notes and architecture material[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Requirements[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFocalDesk is currently developed as a Rust workspace for Linux.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mInstall Rust from <https://rustup.rs/>.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOn Debian/Ubuntu-style systems, the CI environment installs:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```sh[m
[32m+[m[32msudo apt install -y \[m
[32m+[m[32m  pkg-config \[m
[32m+[m[32m  libwayland-dev \[m
[32m+[m[32m  libxkbcommon-dev \[m
[32m+[m[32m  libudev-dev \[m
[32m+[m[32m  libinput-dev \[m
[32m+[m[32m  libegl1-mesa-dev \[m
[32m+[m[32m  libgles2-mesa-dev \[m
[32m+[m[32m  libgbm-dev \[m
[32m+[m[32m  libgtk-4-dev \[m
[32m+[m[32m  libadwaita-1-dev[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Build[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```sh[m
[32m+[m[32mcargo build --workspace[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOr, if you have `just` installed:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```sh[m
[32m+[m[32mjust build[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Check[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```sh[m
[32m+[m[32mcargo fmt --all -- --check[m
[32m+[m[32mcargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings[m
[32m+[m[32mcargo test --workspace[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Run[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe main compositor binary is:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```sh[m
[32m+[m[32mcargo run -p focaldesk-desktop[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBecause FocalDesk is alpha compositor/system software, run it from a safe[m
[32m+[m[32mdevelopment session first. Avoid switching important work over to it until you[m
[32m+[m[32mknow the current state of your local build.[m
[32m+[m
